Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters mandated by the Groundwater Act and matters necessary for the enforcement thereof.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 2 (Survey on groundwater) (1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall conduct a basic survey on the characteristics of groundwater reserves, the exploitable volume of groundwater, the characteristics of groundwater quality, the facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, the outflowing groundwater, etc. throughout the country through geological surveys, geophysical surveys, drilling surveys, and surveys on groundwater levels and water quality in accordance with Article 5(1) of the Groundwater Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"). <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Jan. 6, 2022; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) When the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment conducts a basic survey under paragraph (1), he or she shall make a hydrogeological map drawn on a scale of 1 to 50,000 which includes the following; provided, he or she may make a hydrogeological map drawn on a scale other than 1 to 50,000, where he or she deems it unavoidable in consideration of the content of the survey, etc.: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Topographical and subsurface geological distribution;
  2. Distribution of groundwater levels;
  3. Structure of water-bearing strata and their water supply characteristics;
  4. Characteristics of groundwater quality;
  5. The exploitable volume of groundwater;
  6. Other matters necessary for the basic survey on the characteristics of groundwater reserves.
  (3) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall formulate a plan for surveying groundwater for each region throughout the country every year and shall conduct a basic survey on the characteristics of groundwater reserves and the exploitable volume of groundwater, the characteristics of groundwater quality, the facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, and the outflowing groundwater, etc. according to such plan; provided, he or she may conduct a survey on areas in preference to other areas, in which it is urgently required to develop groundwater as the source of water supply, on which the head of a relevant central administrative agency, or a Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Do Governor, or a Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as the "Mayor/Do Governor") requests for a basic survey. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 30, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Jan. 6, 2022; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) The Minister of Environment shall conduct a complementary survey regarding the following matters in accordance with Article 5(2) of the Act: <Added on Jun. 8, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 16, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Distribution of groundwater levels;
  2. Characteristics of groundwater quality;
  3. The actual conditions of the development and utilization of groundwater;
  4. Other matters necessary for the complementary survey.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 3 (Consultation on survey on groundwater) (1) Where the head of a relevant central administrative agency, the Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu (the head of a Gu means the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply) intends to conduct a survey to perform his or her affairs related to groundwater in accordance with the main clause of Article 5(4) of the Act, he or she shall have a prior consultation with or notify the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment in accordance with the following classifications: <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Jan. 6, 2022; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Where he or she shall hold consultation: Surveys on the matters referred to in Article 2(2)2 through 5;
  2. Where he or she shall give notification: Surveys which do not fall under subparagraph 1.
  (2) Where the head of the relevant central administrative agency, the Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu completes the survey under paragraph (1), he or she shall notify the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment of the results thereof within 1 month from the date he or she completes the survey, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) "Where urgent reasons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 5(4) of the Act means cases where groundwater should be urgently developed and utilized due to war, natural disasters or other accidents. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 4 (Vicarious execution of affairs of surveying) (1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, the head of the relevant central administrative agency, the Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may have any of the following institutions specialized in surveys related to groundwater (hereinafter referred to as "institution specialized in surveys on groundwater") conduct the affairs relating to surveys on groundwater on his or her behalf in accordance with Article 5(5) of the Act: <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Aug. 31, 2021; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. The Korea Institute of Geoscience and Mineral Resources established pursuant to Article 8 of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes;
  2. The Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation under the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act;
  3. The Korea Water Resources Corporation under the Korea Water Resources Corporation Act;
  4. The Korea Rural Community Corporation under the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
  5. The Korea Institute of Construction Technology established pursuant to Article 8 of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes;
  6. The Korea Environment Corporation under the Korea Environment Corporation Act;
  7. The Association established pursuant to Article 26-2 of the Act.
  (2) An institution specialized in surveys on groundwater that vicariously conducts the affairs of surveying groundwater in accordance with Article 5(5) of the Act shall notify the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, the head of the relevant central administrative agency, the Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu of a survey plan within 15 days from the date it commences the survey. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 5 (Request for survey data) (1) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, the head of the relevant central administrative agency, the Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu requests a related agency to submit groundwater survey data or to cooperate with him or her in accordance with Article 5(6) of the Act, he or she shall specify the details of necessary survey data, matters to be cooperated and the deadline for submission of data. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) A related agency requested to submit survey data or to provide cooperation pursuant to paragraph (1) shall comply with such request except in extenuating circumstances.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 6 (Comprehensive management of survey data) (1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall consolidate survey data on groundwater in the whole country, as of December 31 every year, based on surveys on groundwater under Article 5(1) through (3) and (5) of the Act, surveys on the actual conditions of the utilization of groundwater under Article 5(9) of the Act, and other relevant surveys and shall publish an annual groundwater survey report in accordance with Article 5(7) of the Act. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Jan. 6, 2022; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment publishes an annual groundwater survey report in accordance with paragraph (1), he or she shall send such annual report to related agencies to offer it to the general public for their utilization. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 6-2 (Survey on actual conditions of utilization of groundwater) (1) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall conduct a survey on the actual conditions of the utilization of groundwater, including the following matters, each year pursuant to the main clause of Article 5(9) of the Act:
  1. General status of groundwater, such as the location and quantity of groundwater;
  2. Current status of the utilization of groundwater, in terms of users of groundwater, purposes of use, and quantity of used groundwater;
  3. Shapes and characteristics of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, in terms of depth, diameter, and water pumping equipment;
  4. Matters relating to groundwater quality including water testing data referred to in Article 30(5);
  5. Imposition and collection of charges for using groundwater under Article 30-3(1) of the Act.
  (2) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall report the results of surveys on the actual conditions of the utilization of groundwater to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment and the relevant Mayor/Do Governor by March 31 of the following year, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment, in accordance with the main clause of Article 5(9) of the Act. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) The Special Self-Governing City Mayor shall report the results of surveys on the actual conditions of the utilization of groundwater to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment by March 31 of the following year, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment, in accordance with the proviso of Article 5(9) of the Act. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Jan. 6, 2022]
  [Previous Article 6-2 moved to Article 6-3 <Jan. 6, 2022>]

Article 6-3 (Creation and operation of groundwater information system) (1) A groundwater information system under Article 5-2(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "groundwater information system") shall contain the following matters: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. Groundwater survey data under Article 5 of the Act;
  2. Survey data on actual conditions of changes in groundwater under Article 17(1) and (2) of the Act;
  3. Other data related to the utilization and management of groundwater.
  (2) Where necessary for the establishment and operation of a groundwater information system, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may promote standardization for the production, management and distribution of data falling under any of the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) in consultation with related agencies and organizations. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, the Mayors/Do Governors, and the heads of Sis/Guns/Gus shall arrange for related agencies, organizations, and the general public to use information related to surveys on groundwater and the actual conditions of utilization of groundwater among the details of a groundwater information system. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 30, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]
  [Moved from Article 6-2 <Jan. 6, 2022>]

Article 7 (Master plans for management of groundwater) (1) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment deems it necessary to formulate a master plan for the management of groundwater under Article 6(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "master plan"), he or she may request the head of the relevant central administrative agency, the Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu to submit necessary data. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment formulates or revises a master plan, he or she shall publish an announcement of following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. The objectives of a master plan;
  2. The target period of a master plan;
  3. The characteristics of groundwater reserves and the exploitable volume of groundwater;
  4. A plan for survey and utilization of groundwater;
  5. A plan for preservation and management of groundwater;
  6. A plan for water quality management and purification of groundwater;
  7. Other matters prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  (3) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment publicly announces a master plan in accordance with paragraph (2), he or she shall notify the head of the relevant central administrative agency and the Mayor/Do Governor of a master plan without delay. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 30, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) The Mayor/Do Governor notified of a master plan pursuant to paragraph (3) shall send it to the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu, and the head of the Si/Gun/Gu shall provide a master plan for public perusal for at least 20 days; provided, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor shall provide a master plan for public perusal for at least 20 days. <Amended on Oct. 30, 2013>
  (5) "Plan for the quality control and purification of groundwater" in Article 6(1)5 of the Act includes the following: <Amended on Jun. 8, 2018>
  1. Basic direction for a plan for the quality control and purification of groundwater;
  2. The current status and forecast of the pollution of groundwater;
  3. A plan for protection of groundwater quality;
  4. Deleted; <Jan. 6, 2022>
  5. A plan for informatization of groundwater quality;
  6. Other matters necessary for the quality control and purification of groundwater.
  (6) "Other matters concerning the management of groundwater" in Article 6(1)6 of the Act means the following: <Amended on Jun. 8, 2018>
  1. A plan for survey on groundwater and a plan for installation and operation of a groundwater observation network;
  2. A plan for management of groundwater;
  3. A plan for investment in the management of groundwater;
  4. A plan for establishment and operation of a groundwater information system.
  (7) Deleted. <Jun. 8, 2018>
  (8) "Where ... intends to change minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 6(5) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. Where a change is made to the matter prescribed in Article 6(1)2 of the Act according to the results of the survey on the utilization of groundwater under Article 5(9) of the Act;
  2. Where a change is made to the matter prescribed in paragraph (6)3.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jun. 8, 2012]

Article 7-2 (Regional groundwater management plan) (1) The change of a minor matter under the proviso of Article 6-2(1) of the Act means cases falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 7(8). <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012>
  (2) Where the Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu formulates a regional groundwater management plan under Article 6-2(1) or (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "regional management plan") and obtains approval from the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment, he or she shall publish an announcement of the following matters in the public gazette; the same shall also apply where he or she revises the regional management plan: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. The objectives of a regional management plan;
  2. The target period of a regional management plan;
  3. The characteristics of groundwater reserves and the exploitable volume of groundwater;
  4. A plan for the management of water volume and the utilization of groundwater;
  5. A plan for preservation and management of groundwater;
  6. A plan for management of groundwater quality;
  7. Matters concerning the period and place of perusal of related documents;
  8. Reasons for the revision of a regional management plan and the details of revisions (limited to cases where the regional management plan is revised).
  (3) "Where problems in groundwater prescribed by Presidential Decree arise" in Article 6-2(2) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where the source of water is exhausted or ground is subsided because groundwater levels remarkably lower due to the excessive development and use of groundwater;
  2. Where the improvement or purification of water quality is required because the groundwater quality has been deteriorated;
  3. Where seawater has intruded into aquifer due to the excessive development and use of groundwater in coastal areas and insular areas;
  4. Where it becomes impracticable to use groundwater unless other measures necessary for the preservation and management of groundwater are taken.
  (4) A Special Self-Governing City Mayor who has obtained approval for a regional management plan pursuant to Article 6-2(1) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu who has obtained approval for a regional management plan pursuant to Article 6-2(2) of the Act and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu who has been notified of a regional management plan by the Mayor/Do Governor pursuant to paragraph (4) of the aforesaid Article shall provide the details thereof for public perusal for at least 20 days. <Amended on Oct. 30, 2013>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 8 (Application for permission to develop and utilize groundwater) (1) A person who intends to obtain permission for the development and utilization of groundwater under Article 7(1) of the Act or the proviso of Article 8(2) of the Act shall submit an application for permission to the head of a Si (including a Special Self-Governing City Mayor; hereinafter the same shall apply)/Gun/Gu, accompanied by the following documents; provided, where the person applies for permission to develop and utilize groundwater in accordance with the proviso of Article 8(2) of the Act, he or she may omit the submission of documents referred to in subparagraph 1: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 30, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. A land registration map or a forest map showing the location of his or her groundwater development and utilization facilities;
  2. An installation drawing of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater;
  3. A groundwater impact investigation report;
  4. Other documents prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  (2) An installation drawing of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater under paragraph (1)2 shall be prepared by any of the following persons:
  1. An institution specialized in surveys on groundwater;
  2. An engineering business entity in the field of civil engineering of geological features, the foundation, the development of underground resources, the development of water sources, water supply and sewerage, or farming or fishing, who has filed a report pursuant to the Engineering Industry Promotion Act;
  3. A professional engineer in the field of civil engineering of geological features, the foundation, the development of underground resources, the development of water sources, water supply and sewerage, or farming or fishing, who has registered the establishment of an professional engineers' office pursuant to the Professional Engineers Act;
  4. A groundwater impact investigation agency under Article 27(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "groundwater impact investigation agency");
  5. A groundwater purification contractor who has registered pursuant to Article 29-2(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "groundwater purification contractor");
  6. Any agent for investigating environmental impact, who has registered pursuant to Article 15 of the Drinking Water Management Act.
  (3) An installation drawing of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater referred to in paragraph (1)2 shall meet the following standards: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. The upper part of the protection wall beneath the earth's surface shall be installed on the earth's surface; provided, this shall not apply to cases where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems that it is necessary to install the upper part of the protection wall beneath the earth's surface in view of the topographic conditions;
  2. The upper protection facility shall be firmly installed so as not to be damaged, broken or polluted, and a drainageway shall be installed in the upper protection facility;
  3. A notice of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment shall be attached on the upper protection facility.
  (4) Except as provided in paragraph (3), detailed standards for installation of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 8-2 (Purposes of development and utilization of groundwater) A person who intends to develop and utilize groundwater shall indicate purposes of the development and utilization of groundwater that fall under any of the following when he or she makes an application for permission under Article 7(1) of the Act or makes a report under Article 8(1) of the Act, and also indicate whether to be utilized as drinking water when classifying the purposes: <Amended on
  1. Water for living: Groundwater used for daily life, such as for home use, etc.; provided, groundwater falling under subparagraphs 2 and 3 is excluded;
  2. Water for industrial use: Groundwater used for the manufacture of goods and operation of equipment in factories or other manufacturing businesses;
  3. Water for farming or fishing: Groundwater used for agriculture, forestry, livestock or fisheries.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 9 (Examination of groundwater impact investigation reports) (1) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gun receives a groundwater impact investigation report from a person who applies for permission for the development and utilization of groundwater pursuant to Article 7(2) of the Act, he or she shall examine whether the report conforms to the items, method of investigation and assessment standards of a groundwater impact investigation under Article 12(1) and whether the report has been prepared pursuant to guidelines for the preparation thereof and the content to be prepared under Article 12(2). <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012>
  (2) In examining a groundwater impact investigation report pursuant to paragraph (1), where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems it necessary to adjust or supplement the groundwater impact investigation report, he or she may request a person who applies for permission for the development and utilization of groundwater to adjust or supplement the groundwater impact investigation report.
  (3) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems necessary for examining a groundwater impact investigation report pursuant to paragraph (1), he or she may seek opinions from related experts.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 9-2 (Restrictions on permission for development and utilization of groundwater or on volume of groundwater collection) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7(3)4 of the Act means cases where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu is requested to restrict the development and utilization of groundwater by the relevant administrative agency due to reasons, such as impacts on the water volume of a river under the River Act.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 10 Deleted. <Dec. 19, 2001>

Article 11 (Change of permitted matters) (1) "Where a person intends to change matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 7(6) of the Act means the following cases: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021>
  1. Where he or she changes the purposes of development and utilization of groundwater (including a change as to whether to utilize groundwater as drinking water);
  2. Where he or she changes facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater [limited to cases where the groundwater pumping capacity is increased (referring to the maximum water collection volume that he or she may pump up by using the facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, in light of the power unit of the facilities, the diameter and depth of the discharge pipe, etc.; hereinafter the same shall apply)].
  (2) Where a person who has obtained permission for the development and utilization of groundwater in accordance with Article 7(1) of the Act intends to modify any permitted matter, he or she shall file an application for permission for modification, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 12 (Items and methods of groundwater impact investigation) (1) The items, methods and assessment standards of a groundwater impact investigation under Article 7(8) of the Act shall be as specified in Appendix 1; provided, where the head of a Si (including a Special Self-Governing City; hereinafter the same shall apply)/Gun/Gu deems particularly necessary for the preservation of groundwater, he or she may add other items and methods of the groundwater impact investigation, as prescribed by municipal ordinance of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu (referring to an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply), or he or she may comply with the items, methods and assessment standards of the environmental impact investigation under Article 13 of the Drinking Water Management Act. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Oct. 30, 2013>
  (2) Guidelines for the preparation of and the content to be prepared in a groundwater impact investigation report under Article 7(8) of the Act shall be as specified in Appendix 2.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 12-2 (Permission for development and utilization of groundwater in vicinity of river) "Limits prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7-2(1) of the Act means 300 meters.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 12-3 (Extension of term of validity of permission for development and utilization of groundwater) (1) A person who intends to obtain permission for the extension of the term of validity of permission for the development and utilization of groundwater in accordance with Article 7-3(3) of the Act shall file an application for permission for the extension thereof with the head of a Si/Gun/Gu, accompaniend by a groundwater impact investigation report prepared within the last 6 months by not later than 30 days before the expiration date of the term of validity, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment; provided, in cases of developing and utilizing groundwater from geothermal air-conditioning or heating facilities that use geothermy as a source of energy for air-conditioning or heating (hereinafter referred to as "geothermal air-conditioning or heating facilities") (limited to cases where groundwater is subsequently filled into the ground), a groundwater impact investigation report need not be attached. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Nov. 11, 2014; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall notify, in advance, a person who has obtained permission for the development and utilization of groundwater of the procedure for extension and the fact that he or she cannot obtain permission for extension unless he or she applies for extension of the term of validity by not later than six months before the term of validity of permission for the development and utilization of groundwater expires.
  (3) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu may give notification under paragraph (2) by short message service using a mobile phone, electronic mail, fax, or telephone or in writing.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 13 (Reporting on development and utilization of groundwater) (1) Any person who intends to make a report on the development and utilization of groundwater in accordance with the proviso of Article 7(6) of the Act or Article 8(1) of the Act shall submit the following documents to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu; provided, in cases falling under the proviso of Article 7(6) of the Act or Article 8(1)1 of the Act, he or she may omit some of documents to be submitted, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. A land registration map or a forest map showing the location of his or her groundwater development and utilization facilities;
  2. An installation drawing of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater;
  3. Other documents prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  (2) When a person who intends to file a report on the development and utilization of groundwater in accordance with Article 8(1) of the Act prepares an installation drawing of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater referred to in paragraph (1)2, he or she may prepare the installation drawing in accordance with the standard drawing of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) "Below the scale prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 8(1)2 of the Act means cases where the water pumping capacity per day does not exceed 150 tons (limited to cases where the discharge pipe, the inner diameter of which does not exceed 50 millimeters, is used); provided, where the Mayor/Do Governor deems it particularly necessary for the preservation of groundwater or due to the regional conditions, he or she may adjust the water pumping capacity within the limits of 50 percent, as prescribed by municipal ordinance of the relevant Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Do, or Special Self-Governing Province (hereinafter referred to as "City/Do"). <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Oct. 30, 2013>
  (4) "Below the scale prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 8(1)5 of the Act means cases where the water pumping capacity per day does not exceed 100 tons (limited to cases where the discharge pipe, the inner diameter of which does not exceed 40 millimeters, is used); provided, where the Mayor/Do Governor deems it particularly necessary for the preservation of groundwater or due to the regional conditions, he or she may adjust the water pumping capacity within the limits of 50 percent, as prescribed by municipal ordinance of the relevant City/Do.
  (5) In calculating the water pumping capacity under paragraphs (3) and (4), in any of the following cases, the total water pumping capacity shall be summed up:
  1. Deleted; <Nov. 11, 2014>
  2. Where at least two facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater are installed in the same place of business;
  3. Where the same person installs at least two facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater in an area where the distance between the facilities does not exceed 50 meters.
  (6) The change of important matters under the main clause of Article 8(2) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021>
  1. Deleted; <Oct. 30, 2013>
  2. Where the purposes of the development and utilization of groundwater are changed (including a change as to whether to utilize groundwater as drinking water);
  3. Where facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater are changed.
  (7) Any person who intends to file a report on changes pursuant to the main clause of Article 8(2) of the Act shall file a report to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu within one month from the date any reason for such changes occurs.
  (8) Article 8(3) and (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the installation of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater subject to reporting.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 13-2 (Orders to take corrective measures) (1) When the head of a Si/Gun/Gu imposes necessary measures, such as an order to take corrective measures, an order to suspend the utilization of groundwater, or an order to jointly utilize groundwater, against any person who has filed a report on the development and utilization of groundwater pursuant to Article 8(4) of the Act, he or she shall notify the reporting person of the details of such measures in writing, specifying reasons for such order, methods to comply therewith, a compliance period, and other relevant matters. <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  (2) Where the person fails to comply with an order to take the measures within the compliance period under paragraph (1) due to an act of God or any other unavoidable reason, the head of the Si/Gun/Gu may grant an extension of the compliance period within the span of the initial compliance period only once. In such cases, a person who seeks to obtain an extension of such compliance period shall file an application for extension of such period with the head of the Si/Gun/Gu by no later than three days before the initial compliance period ends.
  (3) Where a person notified of an order to take corrective measures, etc. in accordance with paragraph (1) has complied with such order to take corrective measures, etc., he or she shall notify the head of the Si/Gun/Gu of the details thereof within 15 days from the date such order is complied with, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 14 (Reporting on completion of construction works) (1) Deleted. <May 10, 1999>
  (2) Where a person who has obtained permission in accordance with Article 7 of the Act or has made a report in accordance with Article 8 of the Act completes construction works for the installation of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, he or she shall file a report to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu within 1 month from the date the person completes construction works, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu receives a report on completion of construction works under paragraph (2), he or she shall issue a certificate of completion after confirming whether facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater are installed in conformity with the matters permitted or reported within 7 days from the date he or she receives the report, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the location of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater" in Article 9(3) of the Act means the following matters: <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Jun. 8, 2012; Nov. 11, 2014; Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. The location of facilities for development and utilization of groundwater;
  2. Any of the following matters:
  a. The depth and diameter of excavation, a water discharging system, integrating flow meter, and water level measuring pipe, among the details of facilities installed;
  b. A power unit, the inner diameter of discharge pipe, the depth of installation, and the water pumping capacity, among the details of water pumping equipment;
  c. The upper protection hole, the lower protection wall beneath the earth's surface, and the thickness of grouting, among the details of facilities installed to prevent pollution.
  (5) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu issues an order to take corrective measures or takes necessary measures against a person who has reported the completion of construction pursuant to Article 9(3) of the Act, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall notify the person of the details thereof within a specified period not exceeding three months. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Jan. 6, 2022>
  (6) Where the person fails to comply with the order to take the measures within a period under paragraph (5) due to a natural disaster or any other unavoidable reason, the head of the Si/Gun/Gu may grant an extension of the period within the span of the initial compliance period only once. In such cases, a person who seeks to obtain an extension of such compliance period shall file an application for extension of such period with the head of the Si/Gun/Gu by no later than three days before the initial compliance period ends. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011>
  (7) Where a person notified of an order to take corrective measures, etc. in accordance with paragraph (5) has complied with such order to take corrective measures, etc., he or she shall notify the head of the Si/Gun/Gu of the details thereof within 15 days from the date such order is complied with, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [Title Amended on May 10, 1999]

Article 14-2 (Purposes of outflowing groundwater) "Purposes prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 9-2(2) of the Act means the following purposes: <Amended on Nov. 11, 2014; Jan. 21, 2025>
  1. Water for living used for fire-fighting, cleaning, landscaping, construction works, restrooms, parks, or air-conditioning or heating;
  2. Water for industrial use;
  3. Water for farming or fishing;
  4. Other purposes deemed necessary by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 14-3 (Reporting on excavation affecting groundwater) (1) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 9-4(1) of the Act means any of the following matters: <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Nov. 11, 2014>
  1. The depth or diameter of excavation;
  1-2. The planned date of restoration;
  2. The name of a construction company.
  (2) "Acts prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9-4(1)5 of the Act means the following acts: <Amended on Nov. 11, 2014; Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. Exploration under subparagraph 2 of Article 3 of the Mining Industry Act;
  2. Geological or groundwater surveys, the excavation diameter of which exceeds 75 millimeters (excluding cases of national defense and military purposes);
  3. Construction works for geothermal air-conditioning or heating facilities which do not use groundwater.
  (3) "Extent prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9-4(4) of the Act means cases where facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater installed in an area within a radius of 50 meters from the center of a place of excavation in the relevant land fall under any of the following cases: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. Where the maximum volume of groundwater collection per day decreases by at least 20 percent;
  2. Where the groundwater quality fails to meet water quality standards established pursuant to Article 20(2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "water quality standards").
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 14-4 (Post management of facilities for development and utilization of groundwater) (1) Post management under Article 9-5(1) of the Act shall consist of the cleaning, inspection and maintenance of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater.
  (2) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu imposes necessary measures, such as an order to take corrective measures or an order to suspend the utilization of groundwater, against a person who fails to implement post management required under Article 9-5(4) of the Act or who has made a false report, he or she shall notify the person who develops and utilizes the relevant groundwater of the details of the measures within a specified period not exceeding three months. <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  (3) Article 14(6) and (7) shall apply mutatis mutandis to an extension of the compliance period for implementing necessary measures, such as an order to take corrective measures or an order to suspend the utilization of groundwater, imposed under Article 9-5(4) of the Act and to the notification of the results of such implementation, respectively. <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  (4) The sizes and purposes of facilities subject to post management under Article 9-5(5) of the Act shall be as follows, and the inspection interval shall be 2 years; provided, the inspection interval of the facilities falling under subparagraph 4 shall be 5 years: <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Jan. 6, 2022; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Facilities, the water pumping capacity of which exceeds 100 tons a day among the facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater managed by the State or a local government for emergency water supply in preparation for war or other state of emergency;
  2. Facilities, the water pumping capacity of which exceeds 100 tons a day among the facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater for public water supply under Article 19(1);
  3. Facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater for public use prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment, the water pumping capacity of which exceeds 100 tons a day, among the facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater after obtaining permission or approval or filing a report under the Act or other statutes;
  4. Facilities excluding facilities falling under subparagraph 2 or 3 and geothermal air-conditioning and heating facilities, among the facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater permitted pursuant to Article 7(1) of the Act or the proviso to Article 8(2) of the Act.
  (5) Specific methods for the cleaning, inspection, and maintenance of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 14-5 (Installation of facilities for securing groundwater resources) (1) "Areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9-6(1)3 of the Act means the following: <Amended on Jun. 6, 2022>
  1. Areas where groundwater flows out in excess of the standards under Article 9-2(2) of the Act;
  1-2. Areas vulnerable to water supply shortages under Article 9-8 of the Act;
  1-3. Areas where the groundwater levels are identified as being unstable based on the results of surveys on the actual conditions of changes in groundwater levels under Article 17(1) or (2) of the Act;
  2. An area where it is impracticable to secure river water and lake water.
  (2) "Institutions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9-6(4) of the Act means the following institutions: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. The Korea Water Resources Corporation pursuant to the Korea Water Resources Corporation Act;
  2. The Korea Rural Community Corporation pursuant to the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
  3. The Korea Environment Corporation under the Korea Environment Corporation Act.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 8, 2012]

Article 15 (Level of poor water quality) Poor water quality under Article 10(1)6 of the Act and Article 15(1)4 of the Act means cases where groundwater quality is at the level unfit for development and utilization; provided, the water quality of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater for which the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems that a water treatment system is necessary for the purpose of the development and utilization of groundwater is regarded as poor water quality when it is unfit for development and utilization even after water treatment. <Amended on Nov. 11, 2014>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 15-2 (Close scrutiny of changes in groundwater level) Close scrutiny under Article 10(1)8-2 of the Act shall include the following matters: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. Surveys on the surrounding conditions;
  2. Surveys on groundwater levels and quality;
  3. Analysis of causes of changes in groundwater levels or pollution of groundwater;
  4. Other matters necessary for close scrutiny.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 8, 2012]
  [Title Amended on Jan. 6, 2022]

Article 16 (Corrective orders before revocation of permission) (1) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to order any person who develops and utilizes groundwater to take corrective or necessary measures pursuant to Article 10(3) of the Act before he or she revokes permission for the development and utilization of groundwater, he or she shall notify a person who has obtained permission for the development and utilization of the relevant groundwater of the details thereof, within a specified period not exceeding three months.
  (2) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems that there is a natural disaster or any other unavoidable cause, he or she may extend the period notified pursuant to paragraph (1) only once within the limits of the period initially notified. In such cases, a person who intends to extend the period, shall file an application for extension of the period to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu by not later than three days before the period initially notified expires.
  (3) Where a person notified in accordance with paragraph (1) has complied with such order to take corrective measures or other necessary measures, he or she shall notify the head of the Si/Gun/Gu of the details thereof within 15 days from the date such order is complied with, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 17 Deleted. <May 10, 1999>

Article 18 Deleted. <May 10, 1999>

Article 19 (Areas subject to designation of groundwater preservation zones) (1) "Facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater for public water supply prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12(1)3 of the Act means facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater that are utilized to supply groundwater to wide-area waterworks, local waterworks, small-scale waterworks, waterworks for exclusive use or small-scale water-supply systems under Article 3 of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act (hereinafter referred to as "facilities for public water supply"), and "radius prescribed by Presidential Decree" means 50 meters. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011>
  (2) "Areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12(1)7 of the Act means any of the following areas: <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011>
  1. An area in which the preservation of groundwater or restrictions on the development of groundwater is deemed necessary in accordance with a master plan or a regional management plan;
  2. An area in which seawater has already invaded, or is likely to invade, into water-bearing strata due to the excessive development and utilization of groundwater in coastal areas and insular areas;
  3. An area in which the volume of groundwater of facilities for public water supply is likely to decrease due to the installation of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, located within a radius of 100 meters from the center of the facilities for public water supply.
  (3) Deleted. <Nov. 30, 2005>
  (4) "Areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12(7)3 of the Act means an area the designation of which as a groundwater preservation zone is deemed necessary in accordance with a master plan. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Oct. 30, 2013>
  (5) The scope of designation of groundwater preservation zones under Article 12(1) of the Act shall be as specified in Appendix 3. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 19, 2001]

Article 20 (Procedures for designation of groundwater preservation zones) (1) Where the head of the relevant central administrative agency or the head of a Si (excluding a Special Self-Governing City Mayor; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article)/Gun/Gu deems the designation of a groundwater preservation zone under Article 12(1) of the Act or the change of the designation thereof (including the cancellation of designation; hereinafter the same shall apply) necessary, he or she may request the Mayor/Do Governor to designate a groundwater preservation zone or to change the designation thereof, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 30, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Where the head of the relevant central administrative agency or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu requests to designate a groundwater preservation zone or change such designation in accordance with paragraph (1), he or she shall submit a written request, accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Documents stating the purpose of or reasons for designation or change thereof;
  2. Documents stating the details of designation or change thereof;
  3. A topographic map drawn on a scale of 1 to 5,000 or greater, indicating the range and the surface area of an area which he or she intends to designate or to change designation;
  4. A written evidence of land in which the lot number, land category and the surface area of the relevant area are indicated;
  5. Other documents prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  (3) Where the Mayor/Do Governor deems that a request for designation of a groundwater preservation zone or for the change thereof under paragraph (1) is appropriate, he or she shall designate a groundwater preservation zone or change the designation.
  (4) Where the Mayor/Do Governor intends to designate a groundwater preservation zone or change the designation pursuant to Article 12(1) of the Act, he or she shall take the following matters into consideration:
  1. Characteristics of groundwater reserves and the actual conditions of the utilization of groundwater;
  2. Characteristics of quality and polluted conditions of groundwater;
  3. Effects of the development of groundwater on natural ecosystems;
  4. The current status of land use in the relevant area;
  5. The current status of the installation of facilities causing groundwater pollution in the relevant area under Article 26-2(1);
  6. Relevance to any development plan under other statutes and regulations.
  (5) The change of a minor matter under the proviso of Article 12(2) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where the name of a groundwater preservation zone is changed;
  2. Where the surface area of a groundwater preservation zone is increased or decreased within 10 percent of the designated surface area.
  (6) Where the Mayor/Do Governor designates a groundwater preservation zone or make any changes to the designation, he or she shall publish an announcement of the following matters in the public gazette, etc. in accordance with Article 12(5) of the Act: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 30, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. The date of designation of a groundwater preservation zone or the date of change thereof;
  2. The name of a groundwater preservation zone;
  3. The location and the surface area of a groundwater preservation zone;
  4. Reasons for the designation of a groundwater preservation zone or for the change thereof;
  5. Drawings prepared as topographic maps drawn on a scale of 1 to 5,000 or greater;
  6. Other matters prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  (7) The Special Self-Governing City Mayor and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall provide the fact of designation of a groundwater preservation zone or change of the designation thereof, and the details thereof for public perusal for at least 20 days pursuant to Article 12(6) of the Act. <Added on Oct. 30, 2013>
  (8) Where the Mayor/Do Governor designates a groundwater preservation zone or changes the designation, he or she shall publicly notify the land register of such groundwater preservation zone; provided, this shall not apply where he or she cancels the designation of a groundwater preservation zone. <Amended on Oct. 30, 2013>
  (9) Where the Mayor/Do Governor deems that causes referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 12(1) of the Act cease to exist, he or she shall cancel the designation of a groundwater preservation zone. <Amended on Oct. 30, 2013>
  (10) Matters necessary for public notice of the land register under paragraph (8) shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 30, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 20-2 (Hearing opinions of residents) (1) When the Mayor/Do Governor intends to hear opinions of residents regarding the designation of a groundwater preservation zone or change of the designation thereof in accordance with the main clause of Article 12-2(1) of the Act, he or she shall notify the head of the relevant Si (excluding the Mayor of a Special Self-Governing City; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article)/Gun/Gu of a plan for public announcement containing major details of a plan for designation of a groundwater preservation zone or a plan for change thereof. <Amended on Oct. 30, 2013; Nov. 1, 2022>
  (2) A Special Self-Governing City Mayor who intends to hear opinions of residents in accordance with the main clause of Article 12-2(1) of the Act shall publicly announce the major details of a plan for designation of a groundwater preservation zone or a changed plan therefor, and the head of the Si/Gun/Gu notified in accordance with paragraph (1) shall publicly announce the details thereof, as prescribed by municipal ordinance under Article 12-2(2) of the Act. <Amended on Oct. 30, 2013; Nov. 1, 2022>
  (3) Where a Special Self-Governing City Mayor or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu makes a public announcement in accordance with paragraph (2), he or she shall provide such details for the perusal of residents for a period of at least 14 days, as prescribed by municipal ordinance under Article 12-2(2) of the Act. <Added on Nov. 1, 2022>
  (4) A person who holds an opinion on the designation of a groundwater preservation zone or change of the designation thereof publicly announced and publicly perused in accordance with paragraphs (2) and (3) may submit his or her opinion in writing to the Mayor/Do Governor within the period of public perusal. <Amended on Nov. 1, 2022>
  (5) The Mayor/Do Governor shall consider whether to reflect the opinions submitted in accordance with paragraph (4) in the designation of a groundwater preservation zone or change of the designation thereof, and notify those who have submitted the relevant opinions of the result of his or her consideration within 30 days from the expiration date of the period of public perusal. <Amended on Nov. 1, 2022>
  (6) "Minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 12-2(1) of the Act means cases for the correction of errors in the calculation of the surface area of the details of the designation of a groundwater preservation zone or change of the designation thereof. <Amended on Nov. 1, 2022>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 21 (Restrictions on acts within groundwater preservation zones) (1) "Scale prescribed by Presidential Decree or larger" in Article 13(1)1 of the Act means cases where the water pumping capacity per day to be developed and utilized in groundwater preservation zones (excluding any of the following zones) is at least 30 tons. In such cases, where the discharge pipe, the inner diameter of which is at least 32 millimeters is used, the water pumping capacity per day shall be deemed at least 30 tons: <Amended on Nov. 11, 2014>
  1. Zones prescribed in Article 12(1)3 of the Act;
  2. Zones prescribed in Article 19(2)1 of the Act (limited to the zones to preserve the quality of groundwater).
  (2) Article 13(5) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the calculation of the water pumping capacity under paragraph (1).
  (3) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 13(1)2 of the Act, with the exception of its item means facilities subject to permission, approval, reporting, etc. under the Water Environment Conservation Act, the Wastes Control Act, the Chemicals Control Act, the Soil Environment Conservation Act, the Sewerage Act, or the Act on the Management and Use of Livestock Excreta. <Amended on Dec. 9, 2014; Jan. 16, 2018>
  (4) "Acts prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 13(1)3 of the Act means any of the following: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Underground excavation works that are likely to change the flowing route or flowing velocity of groundwater, such as tunneling works;
  2. Installation of a structure that is likely to pollute groundwater, such as underground oil storage, etc.;
  3. Installation of a waste landfill, specific waste storage facilities, cemetery, etc.;
  4. Mining, earth and stone quarrying and breeding and raising livestock, etc., exceeding the size prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment, which can have considerable impact on the quality and quantity of groundwater.
  (5) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to prohibit newly developing and utilizing groundwater in a groundwater preservation zone pursuant to Article 13(2) of the Act, he or she shall announce the following matters in the official report, etc. and open the details of such announcement for public perusal for at least 20 days:
  1. The date of designation of a groundwater preservation zone or the date of change thereof;
  2. The name of a groundwater preservation zone;
  3. The location and the surface area of a groundwater preservation zone;
  4. Drawings prepared as topographic maps drawn on a scale of 1 to 5,000 or greater;
  5. Details of developing and utilizing groundwater prohibited and the period during which such acts are prohibited.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 22 (Amount of performance guarantee and time of deposit) (1) A person who has obtained permission, approval, etc. for or filed a report on the development and utilization of groundwater in accordance with Article 7(1), 8(1), 9-4(1), or 13(1)1 of the Act or another statute shall deposit a performance guarantee under Article 14 of the Act in cash or by a written guarantee, securities, etc. prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment before the commencement date of such construction works. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The amount of a performance guarantee under paragraph (1) shall be used for expenses incurred in restoration to the original state, and specific standards for calculation of the amount of the performance guarantee shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) The period of deposit of a performance guarantee under Article 14(1) of the Act shall be five years from the commencement date of construction works; provided, where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems particularly necessary in consideration of the regional conditions or the conditions of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, he or she may review every five years whether it is necessary to continuously deposit the performance guarantee and have the relevant person keep depositing the performance guarantee. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011>
  (4) Where the period for development and utilization of groundwater is fixed pursuant to Article 7 or 7-3 of the Act or other statutes, notwithstanding paragraph (3), the period of deposit of a performance guarantee shall be until the date one year lapses after the period for development and utilization of groundwater expires. Where the period for development and utilization of groundwater is extended, the period of deposit of a performance guarantee shall be until the date one year lapses after the period for development and utilization of groundwater expires from the date of permission for extension. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011>
  (5) Where a person who is obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state (hereinafter referred to as "person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state") in accordance with Article 15(1) of the Act restores facilities or land to the original state, the period of deposit of a performance guarantee elapses or the relevant area falls under Article 23(1)3, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall return the performance guarantee, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (6) Deleted. <Dec. 19, 2001>
  (7) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu directly restores facilities or land to the original state on behalf of a person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state pursuant to Article 15(4) of the Act, if a performance guarantee does not fully cover the cost of restoration, he or she may charge the person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state for the shortage, and where the balance occurs after he or she uses the performance guarantee, he or she shall return the balance of the performance guarantee, without delay, to the person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011>

Article 22-2 (Exemption from liability to deposit performance guarantee) "Other cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, the restoration of which is deemed certain" in Article 14(1)2 of the Act means cases falling under Article 14-3(2)3.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 23 (Exception to restoration to original state) (1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso, with the exceptions of the subparagraphs, of Article 15(1) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  1. Where a person continues to develop and use groundwater after obtaining permission, approval, etc. or making a report pursuant to the Act or other statutes;
  2. Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems that it is necessary to use facilities or land as a national observation network referred to in Article 17(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "national observation network") or ancillary observation network referred to in paragraph (2) of that Article (hereinafter referred to as "ancillary observation network");
  3. Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems that it is unnecessary to restore facilities or land to the original state under topographical conditions.
  (2) "Other cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, for which the restoration to original state is required" in Article 15(1)8 of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where the ground or a structure subsides or is likely to subside because the groundwater level lowers;
  2. Where groundwater dries up or is likely to dry up because the groundwater level lowers.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 24 (Standards, method, and period of restoration to original state) (1) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu orders a person who develops and utilizes groundwater to restore facilities or land to the original state pursuant to Article 15(2) or (3) of the Act, he or she shall notify a person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state of the details thereof in writing within a fixed period of not more than one month. In such cases, the person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state shall notify the head of a Si/Gun/Gu of the commencement date of restoration to the original state by phone, etc. before he or she commences restoration, and then implement restoration.
  (2) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems that there is a natural disaster or any other unavoidable cause, he or she may extend the period notified pursuant to paragraph (1) up to twice (the period extended each time shall not exceed the limits of the period notified first). In such cases, a person who intends to obtain an extension of the period shall file an application for extension of the period with the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu within three days before the notified period (referring to the extended period, in cases the period has been extended) expires. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2016>
  (3) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall implement restoration on behalf of a person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state pursuant to Article 15(4) of the Act, notify the person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state of the details thereof in writing by not later than seven days prior to the commencement date of restoration.
  (4) Restoration under Article 15 of the Act shall be implemented by the following methods; provided, where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems that it is insufficient to implement restoration by the following methods and determines a method of restoration separately, restoration shall be implemented by such method: <Amended on Jul. 2, 2019>
  1. To check the inner side of the excavation facilities and eliminate the installation materials and polluted materials, fill up from the bottom of original excavation to the ground surface with materials through which water is hard to permeate, such as cement slurry and clay; provided, filling up at the lower part of the protection wall beneath the ground surface (hereafter in this paragraph referred to as "protection wall") may be filled up with materials through which water is easy to permeate, such as sand;
  2. To eliminate the protection wall installed beneath the ground surface; provided, where it is hard to eliminate the protection wall, to cut off the protection wall more than one meter from the ground surface after digging out earth from the around area.
  (5) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall confirm whether or not a person obligated to restore facilities or land to the original state, who has been ordered to implement restoration, implements restoration in conformity with paragraph (4) within a period of restoration.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 25 (Measures to prevent pollution of groundwater) (1) A person who is obligated to take necessary measures, such as the installation of facilities for preventing the pollution of groundwater, (hereinafter referred to as "person obligated to prevent the pollution of groundwater") in accordance with Article 16(1) of the Act shall take measures to prevent the pollution of groundwater in accordance with the following standards: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. He or she shall install the upper protective hole and the protective wall beneath the surface of the earth of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, and maintain a certain degree of slope in the vicinity of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater so that pollutants may not flow into such facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater from the surface of the earth or other facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater; provided, in any of the following cases, he or she may choose not to install the upper protective hole:
  a. Where he or she develops and utilizes groundwater in a building into which no pollutant is likely to flow;
  b. Where he or she has taken measures to prevent the pollution of groundwater under subparagraph 4 when he or she develops and utilizes water for farming or fishing without using any fixed power unit;
  2. Deleted; <Jun. 8, 2012>
  3. Deleted; <Jun. 8, 2012>
  4. He or she shall install the discharge pipe in facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater for farming or fishing, which does not use any fixed power unit, at least 30 centimeters high above the surface of the earth, and make the end portion of the discharge pipe in the form of " ㄱ " and keep it covered in order to prevent any inflow of pollutants;
  5. He or she shall implement other measures determined by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment for preventing the pollution of groundwater.
  (2) Deleted. <Jun. 8, 2012>
  (3) Deleted. <Jun. 8, 2012>
  (4) Deleted. <Jun. 8, 2012>
  (5) Necessary matters regarding detailed standards, etc. for the installation of facilities for preventing the pollution of groundwater under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 26 (Orders to prevent pollution of groundwater) (1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may order any installer or manager of facilities which pollute or are likely to pollute groundwater remarkably to take the following measures to prevent the pollution of groundwater in accordance with Article 16(2) of the Act: <Amended on Jul. 2, 2019; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Installation of a groundwater pollution observation well (a well installed to monitor groundwater pollution and to observe groundwater level, quantity, etc.) and the measurement of groundwater quality;
  2. Assessment of the progress of the pollution of groundwater;
  3. Installation of facilities for preventing the leakage of groundwater pollutants;
  4. Purification of polluted groundwater;
  5. Improvements in equipment and the operation of the relevant facilities;
  6. Deleted; <Jan. 6, 2022>
  (2) Matters necessary for orders to take measures to prevent the pollution of groundwater under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 26-2 (Prevention of pollution of facilities causing groundwater pollution) (1) Any installer or manager (hereinafter referred to as "manager of facilities causing groundwater pollution") of facilities causing groundwater pollution under Article 16-2(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "facilities causing groundwater pollution") shall take the following measures to prevent the pollution of groundwater:
  1. Installation of facilities for preventing the leakage of groundwater pollutants;
  2. Installation of facilities that may confirm whether groundwater pollutants are leaked;
  3. Installation of a groundwater pollution observation well between the upstream and downstream of facilities causing groundwater pollution;
  4. Regular measurements of groundwater quality and reporting the results of measurements of groundwater quality to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu.
  (2) "When the pollution of groundwater prescribed by Presidential Decree occurs or is likely to occur" in the former part of Article 16-2(2) of the Act means the time pollutants are leaked into nearby groundwater in the course of operating facilities causing groundwater pollution.
  (3) When the relevant facilities fall under paragraph (2), the manager of facilities causing groundwater pollution shall take the following measures without delay:
  1. Measurements of groundwater quality under Article 16-2(1) of the Act;
  2. Removal of pollutants;
  3. Installation of facilities for preventing the proliferation of pollutants.
  (4) When the manager of facilities causing groundwater pollution has taken measures under paragraph (3), he or she shall report the following matters to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu without delay: <Amended on Dec. 30, 2016>
  1. Date and time and place of the occurrence of a groundwater pollution accident, and the cause and details of such accident;
  2. The types, concentration and leaked quantity of groundwater pollutants;
  3. Areas likely to be damaged by the pollution of groundwater and a place where groundwater quality has been measured;
  4. Details of various measures taken to control such groundwater pollution accident;
  5. A cadastral map or a forest land map, each drawn on a scale of 1 to 5,000 or greater, indicating the location where a groundwater pollution accident has occurred.
  (5) Matters necessary for methods of installing a groundwater pollution observation well, the interval and method of measurements of water quality, methods of reporting the results of measurements of water quality, etc. under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 26-3 (Measures with respect to managers of facilities causing groundwater pollution) (1) Where groundwater quality does not meet water quality standards prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment under Article 16-3(1) of the Act as a result of the measurement of water quality under Article 16-2(1) of the Act, the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall order the manager of facilities causing groundwater pollution that provides a cause of such pollution to submit a report stating hazards caused by groundwater pollution, the range of pollution, assessment on the cause of such pollution, measures to prevent pollution, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "assessment report on groundwater pollution"), as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall order the manager of facilities causing groundwater pollution to take necessary measures among the following measures, based on an assessment report on groundwater pollution: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Close scrutiny on the range of groundwater pollution;
  2. Installation of additional facilities to prevent the leakage of groundwater pollutants;
  3. Change in the method of transporting, storing and treating groundwater pollutants;
  4. Purification of polluted groundwater;
  5. Improvements in equipment and the operation of the relevant facilities;
  6. A survey on whether polluted groundwater is, or can be, naturally purified by natural decrease in groundwater.
  (3) Guidelines for preparation of an assessment report on groundwater pollution, items to be included, and other necessary matters shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 26-4 (Approval of plans for purifying polluted groundwater) (1) The manager of facilities causing groundwater pollution shall, after preparing a plan for purifying polluted groundwater pursuant to Article 16-4(1) of the Act, obtain approval of such plan from the head of a Si/Gun/Gu not later than 30 days before he or she commences to take measures for purifying polluted groundwater under Article 16-2(2) of the Act or within six months from the date he or she is ordered to purify polluted groundwater under Article 16-3(1) of the Act.
  (2) A plan for purifying polluted groundwater shall contain the following matters:
  1. Methods and types of a purification project;
  2. The period of a purification project and an area where the purification project is undertaken (including the location and surface area of facilities causing groundwater pollution and the range of areas subject to bearing expenses);
  3. The size of a purification project, including the capacity of facilities and the surface area of facilities installed;
  4. The total project costs and the project cost incurred in each field of works;
  5. Methods of raising funds;
  6. Contingency measures where the purification project is not undertaken as scheduled.
  (3) Detailed matters necessary for preparing a plan for purifying polluted groundwater shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 27 (Surveys on actual conditions of changes in groundwater levels) (1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall conduct a survey on the actual conditions of changes in groundwater measured in each national observation network established in accordance with Article 17(1) of the Act; provided, where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs establishes and operates groundwater monitoring networks in areas where groundwater is used for agricultural and fishery purposes under Article 15 of the Agricultural and Fishing Villages Improvement Act, such networks may be utilized instead of establishing national observation networks. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall conduct a survey on the actual conditions of changes in groundwater measured in each ancillary observation network established under Article 17(2) of the Act.
  (3) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall publish an annual groundwater observation report, as of December 31 every year, by consolidating the results of the surveys on actual conditions of groundwater conducted in accordance with paragraph (1) and shall analyze the long-term trends of changes in groundwater. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall determine and publicly notify matters necessary for surveys on the actual conditions of changes in groundwater. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 6, 2022]

Article 28 (Measures against problems with groundwater) (1) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu ascertain that problems under Article 6-2(2) of the Act have arisen in relation to groundwater based on the results of surveys on actual conditions of changes in groundwater conducted under Article 17(1) and (2) of the Act, they shall conduct more detailed surveys on the characteristics of groundwater reserves in the relevant district, the exploitable volume of groundwater, the characteristics of quality of groundwater, the actual conditions of development and utilization of groundwater, and other relevant matters to analyze the causes thereof in accordance with Article 17(5) of the Act. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Where it is deemed necessary to designate the relevant district as a groundwater preservation zone under Article 12(1) of the Act based on the results of surveys conducted under paragraph (1), the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may request the competent Mayor/Do Governor to make such designation in accordance with Article 20(1). <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 6, 2022]

Article 29 (Water quality testing) (1) "Person ... prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20(1) of the Act means a person who develops and utilizes any of the following groundwater; provided, any person who develops and utilizes groundwater for public supply and undergoes water quality testing in accordance with Article 19 of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act shall be excluded: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Drinking water;
  2. Water for living, water for industrial use and water for farming or fishing corresponding to the scale and detailed purposes, etc. prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  (2) A person falling under paragraph (1) shall undergo groundwater quality testing conducted by an institution specialized in testing related to groundwater (hereinafter referred to as "institution specialized in water quality testing") for each period prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. In such cases, where the person develops and utilizes the relevant groundwater for drinking water, he or she shall undergo water quality testing conducted by an inspection agency under Article 30(1)2. <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 30 (Institutions specialized in water quality testing) (1) An institution specialized in water quality testing under Article 20(1) of the Act shall be any of the following institutions: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. An institution specialized in surveys on groundwater;
  2. An inspection agency under Article 43 of the Drinking Water Management Act;
  3. A general waterworks business entity under subparagraph 22 of Article 3 of the Water Supply and Waterworks Installation Act;
  4. The National Institute of Agricultural Sciences in the Rural Development Administration;
  5. A Do agricultural technology institute under the Regulations on Administrative Organizations and the Criteria for the Legally Fixed Number of Officials of Local Governments;
  6. A water quality testing institution prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment where a person who develops and utilizes groundwater develops and utilizes groundwater in facilities installed by national defense and military installation projects.
  (2) Where the result of water quality testing under Article 20(1) of the Act does not meet water quality standards, an institution specialized in water quality testing shall notify the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu of the fact without delay. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) When the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu receives notification under paragraphs (2), he or she may order a person who uses the relevant groundwater to cease the use of such groundwater or to take necessary measures, such as improvements in water quality, by using any of the following methods, in accordance with Article 20(2) of the Act: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Water treatment of groundwater (limited to cases where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems water treatment necessary for the purpose of development and utilization of groundwater);
  2. Complementing facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater.
  (4) Where the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to order to cease the use of groundwater or to take measures, such as improvement in water quality, under paragraph (3), he or she shall notify the relevant person of details of such measures, specified in writing. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) An institution specialized in water quality testing shall keep the records of water quality testing for 2 years and submit the records of water quality testing as of the end of each quarter to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu by the end of the month following the month of the expiration date of each quarter, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 31 (Items for water quality testing) (1) Items for water quality testing under Article 20(3) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. In cases of drinking water: Items established for water quality standards of drinking water under Article 5 of the Drinking Water Management Act;
  2. In cases of water for living, water for industrial use, and water for farming or fishing: Items established for water quality standards of groundwater prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  (2) Methods of water quality testing under Article 20(3) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021>
  1. In cases of drinking water: Water quality testing shall comply with the official test standards for environmental pollution under Article 6(1)6 of the Environmental Testing and Inspection Act;
  2. In cases of water for living, water for industrial use, and water for farming or fishing: Water quality testing shall comply with the official test standards for environmental pollution under Article 6(1)5 of the Environmental Testing and Inspection Act.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 32 (Registration of construction business for development and utilization of groundwater) (1) Any person who intends to make registration of construction business for development and utilization of groundwater in accordance with Article 22(1) of the Act shall submit a written application for registration to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall accept registration, except cases where an application for registration under paragraph (1) falls under any of the following cases:
  1. Where it falls under any of the subparagraphs of Article 23 of the Act;
  2. Where the criteria for registration referred to in Appendix 4 are not met;
  3. Where it violates other restrictions under this Act or other statutes and regulations.
  (3) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu accepts registration in accordance with paragraph (2), he or she shall record registered matters in the register book of construction business for development and utilization of groundwater and issue a certificate of registration to an applicant, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) The criteria for registration of construction business for development and utilization of groundwater under Article 22(1) of the Act shall be as specified in Appendix 4.
  (5) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the trade name or title, among the registered matters" in the latter part of Article 22(1) of the Act means the following: <Amended on Jun. 30, 2016>
  1. The trade name or name;
  2. The representative (excluding the representative of an institution specialized in surveys on groundwater that has registered the construction business for development and utilization of groundwater);
  3. Technical capability, facilities and equipment as specified in Appendix 4;
  4. The relocation of the principal office.
  (6) An application for modification of registration under the latter part of Article 22(1) of the Act shall be filed within one month from the date the reason therefor occurs; provided, where the technical capability is changed, an application for modification of registration shall be filed within 50 days from the date the reason therefor occurs. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 33 Deleted. <May 10, 1999>

Article 34 (Exceptions to construction works of facilities for development and utilization of groundwater) "Other insignificant construction works prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22(2)2 of the Act means any of the following construction works:
  1. Restoration works of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater, the water pumping capacity of which is less than 30 tons a day and the diameter of excavation of which does not exceed 75 millimeters;
  2. Maintenance works of the upper protection hole (including the replacement and repair of the integrating flowmeter and flushing device) of facilities for the development and utilization of groundwater;
  3. Construction works of a geothermal air-conditioning or heating facility not using groundwater.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 35 (Reporting on transfer and takeover of construction business for development and utilization of groundwater) (1) A person who intends to file a report in accordance with Article 24(1) or (2) of the Act shall submit a written report in the form prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment, accompanied by documents prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment, to the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Upon receipt of a report under paragraph (1), the head of the Si/Gun/Gu shall examine whether it meets the standards for registration specified in Appendix 4 and whether it falls under any of the grounds for disqualification specified in the subparagraphs of Article 23 of the Act.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 6, 2022]

Article 36 (Continued construction after having been subject to disposition of cancellation of registration) Where any construction contractor for development and utilization of groundwater who has been subject to disposition of cancellation of registration pursuant to Article 25(2) of the Act intends to continue construction works which he or she commenced before he or she is subject to such disposition, he or she shall notify without delay the owner of construction works and the head of a Si/Gun/Gu who has jurisdiction over the area where construction works are performed of the fact that his or her registration has been cancelled.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 37 (Procedures for revocation of registration of construction business for development and utilization of groundwater) (1) Deleted. <May 10, 1999>
  (2) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu revokes registration pursuant to Article 25(1) of the Act, he or she shall publicly announce the fact of cancellation in the official report, etc. without delay and notify the person concerned thereof. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011>
  (3) Other matters necessary for procedures for revocation of registration of construction business for development and utilization of groundwater shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [Title Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 38 (Criteria for registration of groundwater impact investigation agencies) (1) A person who is eligible to register as a groundwater impact investigation agency pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act shall be any of the following persons and shall have the technical capability, facilities and equipment referred to in Appendix 5:
  1. An institution specialized in surveys on groundwater;
  2. An engineering business entity in the field of geological features, foundation, development of water resources, water supply and sewerage, or civil engineering for agriculture or fishery, who has reported pursuant to the Engineering Industry Promotion Act;
  3. A professional engineer's office established and registered by a professional engineer in the field of geological features, foundation, development of water resources, water supply and sewerage, or civil engineering for agriculture or fishery pursuant to the Professional Engineers Act;
  4. A research institute related to natural (physical) science or engineering of a school under subparagraphs 1 through 6 of Article 2 of the Higher Education Act;
  5. An agent for environmental impact investigation designated pursuant to the Drinking Water Management Act;
  6. Other corporations which conduct affairs related to groundwater.
  (2) A person who intends to register as a groundwater impact investigation agency in accordance with Article 27(1) of the Act shall submit a written application for registration to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall accept registration, except cases where an application for registration under paragraph (2) falls under any of the following cases:
  1. Where it falls under any of the subparagraphs of Article 28 of the Act;
  2. Where it fails to meet the criteria for registration referred to in paragraph (1);
  3. Where it violates other restrictions under this Act or other statutes and regulations.
  (4) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu accepts registration of a groundwater impact investigation agency in accordance with paragraph (3), he or she shall record the registered matters in the register book of groundwater impact investigation agencies and issue a certificate of registration to an applicant, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) An application for modification of registration under the latter part of Article 27(1) of the Act shall be filed within one month from the date the reason therefor occurs; provided, where the technical capability is changed, an application for modification of registration shall be filed within 50 days from the date the reason therefor occurs. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012>
  (6) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the trade name or name, among the registered matters" in the latter part of Article 27(1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Jun. 30, 2016>
  1. The trade name or name;
  2. The representative (excluding the representative of an institution specialized in surveys on groundwater registered as a groundwater impact investigation agency);
  3. Technical capability, facilities and equipment specified in Appendix 5;
  4. The relocation of the principal office.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 39 (Cancellation of registration of groundwater impact investigation agencies) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu cancels registration pursuant to Article 29(1) of the Act, he or she shall publicly announce the fact of cancellation in the official report, etc. and notify the person in question of the fact without delay.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 39-2 (Registration of groundwater purification business) (1) A person who intends to register his or her groundwater purification business in accordance with Article 29-2(1) of the Act shall fall under any of the subparagraphs of Article 38(1), have the technical capability, capital, facilities and equipment referred to in Appendix 6 and submit an application for registration to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall accept registration, except cases where an application for registration under paragraph (1) falls under any of the following cases:
  1. Where it falls under any of the subparagraphs of Article 23 of the Act;
  2. Where it fails to meet the criteria for registration referred to in Appendix 6;
  3. Where it violates other restrictions under this Act or other statutes and regulations.
  (3) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu accepts registration in accordance with paragraph (2), he or she shall record registered matters in the register book of groundwater purification business and issue a certificate of registration to an applicant, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the trade name or name, among the registered matters" in the latter part of Article 29-2(1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on Jun. 30, 2016>
  1. The trade name or name;
  2. The representative (excluding the representative of an institution specialized in surveys on groundwater registered as the groundwater purification business);
  3. Technical capability, facilities and equipment under Appendix 6;
  4. The relocation of the principal office.
  (5) An application for modification of registration under the latter part of Article 29-2(1) of the Act shall be filed within one month from the date the reason therefor occurs; provided, where the technical capability is changed, an application for modification of registration shall be filed within 50 days from the date the reason therefor occurs. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012>
  (6) "Insignificant purification works prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 29-2(2) of the Act means purification works performed when the water quality of groundwater to be purified does not exceed 110/100 of water quality standards.
  (7) Article 35 through 37 shall apply mutatis mutandis to groundwater purification business. In such cases, "construction business for development and utilization of groundwater" shall be construed as "groundwater purification business", and "construction contractor for development and utilization of groundwater" shall be construed as "groundwater purification contractor", respectively.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 40 (Groundwater management committee) (1) Deleted. <Apr. 30, 2009>
  (2) A regional groundwater management committee may be established in each City/Do in order to provide advice and suggestions as requested by the Mayor/Do Governor concerning the following matters: <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Jun. 8, 2012; Oct. 30, 2013>
  1. Matters concerning the formulation of a regional management plan and a revised regional management plan under Article 6-2(1) of the Act;
  2. Matters concerning consultation on a regional management plan of a Si/Gun/Gu under Article 6-2(2) of the Act (excluding cases of a regional groundwater management committee established in a Special Self-Governing City);
  3. Matters concerning the designation of a groundwater preservation zone and the change thereof under Article 12(1) of the Act;
  4. Matters referred to in paragraph (3)2 through 4 (only applicable to cases of a regional groundwater management committee established in a Special Self-Governing City);
  5. Other matters concerning the development and utilization, and the preservation and management of groundwater, referred to a conference by the Mayor/Do Governor.
  (3) A regional groundwater management committee may be established in each Si (excluding a Special Self-Governing City; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article)/Gun/Gu in order to provide advice and suggestions as requested by the head of a Si (excluding the Mayor of a Special Self-Governing City; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article)/Gun/Gu concerning the following matters: <Amended on Dec. 30, 2011; Jun. 8, 2012; Oct. 30, 2013>
  1. Matters concerning the formulation of a regional management plan and the modification thereof under Article 6-2(2) of the Act;
  2. Matters concerning a groundwater impact investigation report under Article 7(2) of the Act;
  3. Matters concerning an assessment report on groundwater pollution under Article 26-3(1);
  4. Matters concerning a plan for purifying polluted groundwater under Article 26-4;
  5. Other matters concerning the development and utilization, and the preservation and management of groundwater, referred to a conference by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu.
  (4) Except as provided in paragraphs (2) and (3), matters necessary for the organization and functions of the regional groundwater management committee under paragraphs (2) and (3) and the operation thereof, such as the exclusion of, challenge to, recusal or discharge of its members, shall be prescribed by ordinance of the relevant City/Do or Si/Gun/Gu; provided, where a committee having characteristics and functions similar to those of the regional groundwater management committee has been established in the relevant City/Do or Si/Gun/Gu and its members meet the qualifications prescribed by municipal ordinance under the main clause, it may replace the functions of the regional groundwater management committee, as prescribed by ordinance of the relevant City/Do or Si/Gun/Gu. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Dec. 29, 2017>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 19, 2001]

Article 40-2 (Establishment of special account for groundwater management) (1) "Purposes prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-2(4)11 of the Act means the following purposes: <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Jan. 6, 2022; Nov. 25, 2025>
  1. Conducting a groundwater impact investigation under Article 8(4) of the Act;
  2. Implementation of an investigation for the designation of a groundwater preservation area under Article 12 of the Act (applicable only when conducted by a Special Self-Governing City Mayor);
  3. Implementation of examinations and investigations of each of the following subparagraphs; provided, in the case of item a through c, applicable only when conducted by the Special Self-Governing City Mayor;
  a. Quality examination of drinking water, spring water and saline groundwater under Article 5(2) of the Drinking Water Management Act;
  b. Quality examination of drinking spring water. etc. (referring to drinking spring water or drinking saline groundwater under subparagraphs 3 and 3-3 of Article 3 of that Act; hereinafter the same shall apply), among examinations under Article 26(4) of the Drinking Water Management Act;
  c. Investigation of compliance with water quality standards for drinking spring water, etc. among investigations under Article 41-2(1) of the Drinking Water Management Act;
  d. Quality examination of drinking water under subparagraph 1 of Article 3 of the Drinking Water Management Act, among examinations under Article 42(1)2 of that Act;
  4. Management of public drinking water facilities under Article 8(1) of the Drinking Water Management Act;
  5. Designation and operation of spring water preservation areas under Article 8-3 of the Act (applicable only when conducted by a Special Self-Governing City Mayor);
  6. Examination of a groundwater impact investigation report under Article 9;
  7. Implementation of a basic survey and restoration works for the development, utilization, preservation, and management of groundwater resources;
  8. Other purposes prescribed by ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu for the preservation and management of groundwater.
  (2) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu formulates a plan for the use of the special accounts for groundwater management including the following matters pursuant to Article 30-2(6) of the Act, he or she shall report the details thereof by the end of February every year, and where he or she revises a plan for the use of the special accounts for groundwater management he or she has formulated, he or she shall report the details thereof within one month from the date he or she revises such plan: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 30, 2013>
  1. The size of the special account for the management of groundwater;
  2. The revenue and expenditure of the previous year;
  3. A business plan of the year concerned;
  4. A plan for repayment of loans;
  5. Other matters regarding the management of the special account for groundwater management.
  (3) "Change of minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 30-2(6) of the Act means the change of the matters falling under paragraph (2)5 among a plan for the operation of the special account for groundwater management that has been formulated. <Amended on Oct. 30, 2013>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 40-3 (Subjects of imposition of charges for using groundwater) (1) The subjects of imposition of charges for using groundwater under Article 30-3(1)2 of the Act are as follows: <Added on Nov. 25, 2025>
  1. Spring water and saline groundwater Act under subparagraphs 2 and 3-2 of Article 3 of the Drinking Water Management Act (hereinafter referred to as "spring water, etc.") collected by the following person who has obtained permission for development in accordance with Article 9 of that Act:
  a. Spring water, etc. collected by a person who has obtained permission for development for other spring water under Article 3(1)2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Drinking Water Management Act;
  b. Spring water, etc. collected by a person who uses manufacturing facilities for drinking spring water, etc. to manufacture beverages;
  2. Spring water, etc. collected by a person who has obtained permission for manufacturing business of drinking spring water, etc. in accordance with Article 21(1) of the Drinking Water Management Act;
  3. Drinking spring water, etc. imported by a person registered to engage in import-sale business of drinking spring water, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "import-sale business operator of drinking spring water") in accordance with Article 21(3) of the Act.
  (2) Any of the following subjects of the imposition of charges under paragraph (1) shall be exempt from the charges for using groundwater under Article 30-3(1)2 of the Act: <Added on Nov. 25, 2025>
  1. For export;
  2. For supply to foreign armed forces or foreign diplomatic missions in Korea;
  3. For supply and provision for the aid of victims of disaster in accordance with Article 66(3)1 of the Framework Act on the Management of Disasters and Safety;
  4. Spring water, etc. collected for an environmental impact survey under Article 13(1) of the Drinking Water Management Act or for an environmental impact examination under Article 18(1) of that Act.
  (3) A person falling under each subparagraph of paragraph (1) shall submit to the Mayor/Do Governor, on a quarterly basis, documents evidencing exemption from the imposition of charges for using groundwater in accordance with paragraph (2), as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Added on Nov. 25, 2025>
  (4) "Purposes and ... scale prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-3(2)5 of the Act means the following cases: <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Nov. 11, 2014; Dec. 30, 2016; Nov. 25, 2025>
  1. Where a kindergarten under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Early Childhood Education Act, a school under Article 2 of the Elementary and Secondary Education Act or Article 2 of the Higher Education Act, and its affiliated facilities develop and utilize groundwater;
  2. Where social welfare facilities under Article 34 of the Social Welfare Services Act develop and utilize groundwater;
  3. Where groundwater is developed and utilized for domestic use (limited to facilities used to run household management) among water for living;
  4. Where groundwater is developed and utilized as a small-scale water supply system in an area where tap water is not supplied;
  5. Where a geothermal air-conditioning or heating facility develops and uses groundwater (limited to cases where groundwater is filled into the ground again);
  6. Cases prescribed by municipal ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu, other than the cases falling under subparagraphs 1 through 5.
  (5) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to reduce or exempt charges for using groundwater under Article 30-3(1)1 of the Act in accordance with Article 30-3(2) of the Act, he or she shall consider the following matters: <Added on Jan. 6, 2022; Nov. 25, 2025>
  1. The purposes of the development and utilization of groundwater;
  2. The quantity of groundwater used compared with the exploitable volume of groundwater;
  3. Whether alternative water sources can be used;
  4. Ability to bear charges for using groundwater.
  (6) The detailed standards for the reduction of, or exemption from, charges for using groundwater under paragraph (5) shall be prescribed by ordinance of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu, taking into account the matters specified in each subparagraph of that paragraph. <Added on Jan. 6, 2022; Nov. 25, 2025>
  (7) "Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the items, of Article 30-3(3)2 of the Act means 1,320 won per cubic meter. <Added on Nov. 25, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]
  [Title Amended on Nov. 25, 2025]

Article 40-4 (Procedures for imposition and collection, and deadline of payment of charges for using groundwater) (1) The Mayor/Do Governor shall, when imposing and collecting charges for using groundwater under Article 30-3(1)2 of the Act, compute charges and issue a payment notice by 10th of the month following the month beginning the next quarter, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  (2) The payment deadline of charges for using groundwater under paragraph (1) shall be the end of the month in which a payment notice has been issued.
  (3) An import-sale business operator of drinking spring water, etc. shall submit to the Mayor/Do Governor a quarterly actual import record by the end of the month when the next quarter begins, as prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment.
  [This Article Added on Nov. 25, 2025]

Article 40-5 (Additional charges) "Additional charges prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-3(6) of the Act means an amount equal to 1/1,000 of the charges for using groundwater in arrears multiplied by the number of days corresponding to the period from the day after the deadline for payment to the day before the deadline for payment. In such cases, the period for collecting the additional charges shall not exceed 30 days.
  [This Article Added on Nov. 25, 2025]

Article 40-6 (Subjects for calculation of payments to Si/Gun/autonomous Gu) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-3(8) of the Act means persons who have obtained permission for development in accordance with Article 9 of the Drinking Water Management Act and have collected spring water, etc. classified under Article 40-3(1)1a and b, and persons who have collected spring water, etc. under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph.
  [This Article Added on Nov. 25, 2025]

Article 40-7 (Deferment of collection or installment payment of charges for using groundwater) (1) The deferred period of collection under Article 30-5(1) of the Act shall be not more than 2 years from the date following the date of such deferment, and the number of installments within the grace period shall be not more than 12 times.
  (2) Any person who intends to have the collection of groundwater usage charges deferred or to pay such charges in installments in accordance with Article 30-5(1) of the Act shall submit an application for deferment of collection or an application for payment in installments prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment to either of the following persons no later than 3 days before the deadline for payment:
  1. In the case of charges for using groundwater under Article 30-3(1)1 of the Act: The head of a Si/Gun/Gu;
  2. In the case of charges for using groundwater under Article 30-3(1)2 of the Act: The Mayor/Do Governor.
  (3) The Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu, when he or she grants deferment of collection or payment in installments in accordance with Article 30-5(1) of the Act, shall notify the applicant in writing of the amount of money deferred, deferment period, amount of money to be paid in installments, payment period, and other necessary matters.
  (4) The decision of deferment of collection or payment in installments shall come into effect on the date of submission of an application in accordance with paragraph (2).
  (5) When deferment of collection or payment in installments is granted to an applicant, a payment notice shall be issued so that it can be delivered to an applicant 15 days prior to the payment due date.
  (6) The provisions of Articles 65 through 70 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes apply mutatis mutandis to providing security for payment under Article 30-5(1) of the Act.
  [This Article Added on Nov. 25, 2025]

Article 41 (Permission for access to land) A person who intends to obtain permission to temporarily use land of another person or to alter or remove bamboos and trees, earth and stones or other obstacles pursuant to Article 31(3) of the Act shall submit to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu a written application stating the seat, lot number, land category, area, the current conditions of land which he or she should have access to or use, the name and address of the owner or occupant, and the purpose, time and period of access and use, accompanied by drawings.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 42 (Education) (1) Those subject to education and training under Article 34-2(2) of the Act shall be as follows:
  1. Technical manpower of a construction contractor for the development and utilization of groundwater falling under subparagraph 1 of Appendix 4;
  2. Technical manpower of a groundwater impact investigation agency falling under subparagraph 1 of Appendix 5;
  3. Technical manpower of a groundwater purification contractor falling under subparagraph 1 of Appendix 6.
  (2) The content of education and training under Article 34-2(2) of the Act shall contain the following matters:
  1. Laws and policies on groundwater;
  2. Technologies on the development, preservation and management of groundwater;
  3. Other matters necessary for the appropriate development and utilization, and preservation and management of groundwater.
  (3) Those subject to education and training under paragraph (1) shall receive education and training within one year from the date they register pursuant to Article 22(1), 27(1) and 29-2(1) of the Act; provided, where those subject to education and training of an institution specialized in surveys on groundwater receive in-house education and training including matters referred to in paragraph (2), they shall be deemed to receive education and training under Article 34-2(2) of the Act.
  (4) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment may entrust the following agencies and organizations with the affairs of education and training under Article 34-2(2) of the Act in accordance with Article 34-2(3) of the Act: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. The Korea Water Resources Corporation pursuant to the Korea Water Resources Corporation Act;
  2. The Korea Rural Community Corporation pursuant to the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act;
  3. The Association established pursuant to Article 26-2 of the Act.
  (5) The head of an institution specialized in surveys on groundwater conducting in-house education and training in accordance with the proviso of paragraph (3) and the head of an agency or organization entrusted with the affairs of education and training in accordance with paragraph (4) shall submit an education plan of the following year including the matters referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraph (2) to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment every year, and submit the result of education of the relevant year to the Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment by January 30 of the following year. <Amended on Jun. 8, 2012; Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (6) Except as provided in this Decree, necessary matters regarding the period of education, etc. shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

Article 43 (Delegation of authority) (1) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall delegate the following authority to the head of the competent flood control office in accordance with Article 36(1) of the Act: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jun. 8, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Consultation on the development and utilization of groundwater in the vicinity of a river under Article 7-2(1) of the Act;
  2. Request for restrictions on the water collection volume and the period for collecting water, and prohibition on the collection of groundwater pursuant to the former part of Article 7-2(2) of the Act;
  3. Requesting an applicant for permission for the development and utilization of groundwater to obtain consent from the person who is currently using a river, pursuant to the latter part of Article 7-2(2) of the Act.
  (2) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall delegate the following authority to the head of a regional environmental management office in accordance with Article 36(1) of the Act: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. An order to take measures for preventing the pollution of groundwater under Article 16(2) of the Act;
  1-2. An order to take measures under Article 16(3) of the Act;
  2. An order to take measures under Article 16-3(1) and (2) of the Act;
  3. Surveys on the actual conditions of the pollution of groundwater under Article 17(1) of the Act;
  4. An order to take measures, such as the suspension of the utilization of groundwater or improvement in water quality, under Article 20(2) of the Act.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jun. 8, 2012]

Article 43-2 (Re-examination of regulation) The Minister of Climate, Energy and Environment shall examine the appropriateness of the subjects and amounts of charges for using groundwater under Article 40-3(1), (2), and (7) every 3 years, counting from January 1, 2024 (referring to the period that ends on the day before January 1 of every third year) and shall take measures, such as making improvements.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Mar. 24, 2026]

Article 43-3 (Processing of personally identifiable information) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu may process data that include resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers under subparagraph 1 or 4 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act, where it is essential for conducting the following administrative affairs: <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022; Nov. 25, 2025>
  1. Administrative affairs regarding the report on the change of a plan for using groundwater runoff under the latter part of Article 9-2(2) of the Act;
  2. Administrative affairs regarding confirmation of the grounds for disqualification under Article 23 of the Act for the registration of construction business for development and utilization of groundwater or a change therein under Article 22(1) of the Act;
  3. Administrative affairs regarding confirmation of the grounds for disqualification under Article 28 of the Act for the registration of groundwater impact investigation agencies or a change therein under Article 27(1) of the Act;
  4. Administrative affairs regarding confirmation of the grounds for disqualification under Article 23 of the Act, which is applicable mutatis mutandis in accordance with paragraph (3) of that Article, for the registration of groundwater purification business or a change therein under Article 29-2(1) of the Act;
  5. Administrative affairs regarding the imposition and collection of charges for using groundwater under Article 30-3(1) of the Act.
  [This Article Added on Nov. 11, 2014]

Article 44 (Criteria for imposition of administrative fines) The Criteria for the imposition of administrative fines under Articles 39, 40, and 40-2 of the Act shall be as specified in Appendix 7. <Amended on Jan. 6, 2022>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 30, 2011]

